+/* Emit the CIE that this translation unit's FDEs share.
+
+   This runs on demand, at the first FDE, rather than once at session start.
+   A CIE describes how to unwind the frames its FDEs cover, so a CIE with no
+   FDE after it describes nothing: emitting one unconditionally left an
+   .eh_frame section on output that contains only an orphan CIE whenever tcc
+   produced no FDEs at all -- assembling a .S file, most visibly, where gas
+   emits no .eh_frame section whatsoever.
+
+   Deferring it also means the section is only reached for once tcc actually
+   has unwind data to put in it, so an .eh_frame arriving from input is left
+   alone in the common case, and when tcc does emit, the CIE is appended after
+   whatever input content is already present.  That is well-formed: .eh_frame
+   is a chain of self-delimiting records, and an FDE identifies its CIE by the
+   distance back to it (see the CIE Pointer in tcc_debug_frame_end), so records
+   from different producers coexist in one section. */
